208	## 4. Finding 3: `ownGeneric`'s comment
209	
210	On `main` (`OverloadedFunction.java:2235-2238`): "A functional method of a generic trait is instantiated from its self argument, and a generic dotted method has no symbolic instantiation to read its declared domain from; both are compared on the instance a call makes."
211	
212	- Rung W's `methodDeclaredBelow` reads a symbolic instance's domain as its declared domain (`:2173-2180`). `preferredDeclaration` then compares a generic dotted method on it wherever exactly one of the two declared domains lies inside the other (`:2154-2168`). So the second half is false of dispatch as a whole.
213	- The sentence stays true of `ownGeneric` itself and of `moreSpecificDeclaration`, as W's report says (`explorations/compile-ladder/rung-walk-method-sargs/REPORT.md:155`).
214	- By section 3's reading, "of a generic trait" also leaves out a generic object.
215	
216	W was right to leave it: `ownGeneric` belongs to G's load check, and no two rungs change one declaration. G's report scoped its own check by that comment as its branch held it (`explorations/compile-ladder/rung-walk-generic-pairs/REPORT.md:155`), which was true there. The comment lands half false.
217	
218	Correcting it edits a path the gate reads (`climb-batch-workflow.js:1444-1446`), so it goes to the next batch that edits `OverloadedFunction.java`, with this text for the comment:
