220	    A declaration whose own static parameters a call's arguments
221	    instantiate: a generic function or constructor, or a functional method
222	    with static parameters of its own in a trait or object that has none.
223	    A functional method of a generic trait or object is instantiated from
224	    its self argument and compared on the instance a call makes; so is a
225	    generic dotted method here, which preferredDeclaration compares on its
226	    declared domain where exactly one of two declared domains lies inside
227	    the other.
